  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The distance between two stars of masses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>. Here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the mean distance between the centres of the Earth and the Sun, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is the mass of the Sun. Two stars orbit around their common centre of mass in circular orbits with period&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, where<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;is the period of Earth&#39;s revolution around the Sun.</p><p>The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>For binary stars,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>G</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>G</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>9</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>T</mi></math></p><p>Value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.</p>",
